-- הסכם קיבוצי מיום 18.3.2020 — התפשטות נגיף הקורונה: פתרונות לעובדים שנאסר
-- עליהם להגיע לעבודה: the public-sector agreement of the first corona
-- lockdown, between the State (and the defence plants), the Centre of Local
-- Government, the three large cities, the regional councils, the religious
-- councils, the National Insurance Institute, the Employment Service and
-- the seven research universities, and the New General Histadrut. Whom it
-- covers, another public employer by an accession letter (§2); its period,
-- 19.3.2020–16.4.2020, subject to legislation (§3); the essential worker,
-- the manager, the public employer and the regular employee (§4); every
-- regular employee on vacation leave for the period — out of his balance,
-- or as an advance on days to come — with no sick pay, and the days he may
-- be called back for in July–August 2020 in their place (§5); a vacation-days
-- fund at each employer (§6); the follow-up committee (§7); the government's
-- intention to legislate (§8). Annexed: the form of the accession letter.
--
-- It covers no teaching employee: it reaches an employee "represented by
-- the Histadrut" (§2(א)), and the teaching scale is represented by הסתדרות
-- המורים and ארגון המורים (the Collective Agreements Law, §§15–16,
-- imported). The emergency regulations that extended it to the wider
-- public sector, and stood aside for "another agreement" approved by the
-- wages commissioner, are outside the corpus; the teachers' instruments of
-- the same weeks are the circulars תש"פ/5, תש"פ/6 (the colleges' special
-- agreement of 31.3.2020) and תש"פ/7 (the State teachers' special agreement
-- of 1.4.2020), held against this one in l4/tests/2019-20_tashaf_07-tests.l4.
-- The agreement of 16.9.2020 recites it and imports this file. It speaks to
-- no pay item of l4/lib/vocabulary.l4 and is in no root.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT parties
IMPORT conventions
IMPORT vocabulary
IMPORT collective_agreements_law
IMPORT budget_foundations_law
IMPORT sick_pay_law
IMPORT annual_leave_law
IMPORT womens_work_law

§ `הסכם קיבוצי — התפשטות נגיף הקורונה: פתרונות לעובדים שנאסר עליהם להגיע לעבודה (18.3.2020)`

DECLARE `2020 furlough action` IS ONE OF
    `sign the accession letter to the agreement of 18.3.2020`
    `call the employee to work in July–August 2020 in place of the furlough days`
    `ask that the agreement of 18.3.2020 apply to employees sent on unpaid leave the week before`
    `set up a vacation-days fund under the agreement of 18.3.2020`
    `decide disputes over the agreement of 18.3.2020`
    `discuss a sick note of hospitalisation or serious illness in the furlough period`
    `act to legislate the agreement of 18.3.2020`

-- akn:preamble The agreement's frame: a label row with no text of its own.
-- akn:preamble/p1 The document's title; no rule.
-- akn:preamble/p3 The registration stamp: registered on 15.6.2020, number 7012 + 113/2020; no rule.
-- akn:preamble/p4 The corpus's note on the initials in the margins of the pages; no rule.
-- akn:preamble/p5 "Between"; no rule.
-- akn:preamble/p20 The employers' short name; no rule.
-- akn:preamble/p21 "On the one side"; no rule.
-- akn:preamble/p22 "And"; no rule.
-- akn:preamble/p23 The New General Histadrut and who represents it; no rule.
-- akn:preamble/p24 The Histadrut's short name; no rule.
-- akn:preamble/p25 "On the other side"; no rule.
-- akn:preamble/p26 A recital: fighting the spread of the corona virus needed special instructions that bear on the whole economy and the public sector's employees.
-- akn:preamble/p27 A recital: those instructions restrict workplaces opening and employees coming to work, and make ordinary work impossible.
-- akn:preamble/p28 A recital: the parties sought solutions for employees barred from coming to work who cannot go on working as usual.
-- akn:preamble/p29 A recital: the parties recognise the need to protect public health and the employees' health.
-- akn:preamble/p30 A recital: in place of suspending the contracts of employment, a temporary arrangement keeping employment continuous and giving certainty.
-- akn:preamble/p31 A recital: the parties set down their understandings in this collective agreement.
-- akn:preamble/p32 The words of agreement that introduce the clauses; no rule.

-- ¶2: signed on 18 March 2020.
@ref akn:preamble/p2
`the 2020 furlough agreement was signed on` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 18 3 2020

-- ¶6–¶19: the employers that sign ("המעסיקים"): the State — and, for the
-- employees of the plants serving the defence system to whom §2(6) of the
-- State Service (Appointments) Law applies, those empowered to sign for
-- them; the Centre of Local Government for every local authority but the
-- three large cities; the three large cities; the Centre of Regional
-- Councils for its members; the religious councils' union; the National
-- Insurance Institute; the Employment Service; and the Hebrew University,
-- Bar-Ilan, Ben-Gurion, Haifa, Tel Aviv, the Technion and the Weizmann
-- Institute (whose representatives' names are left blank).
@ref akn:preamble/p6 akn:preamble/p7 akn:preamble/p8 akn:preamble/p9 akn:preamble/p10 akn:preamble/p11 akn:preamble/p12 akn:preamble/p13 akn:preamble/p14 akn:preamble/p15 akn:preamble/p16 akn:preamble/p17 akn:preamble/p18 akn:preamble/p19
`the employers that signed the agreement of 18.3.2020` MEANS
    LIST "מדינת ישראל (לרבות המפעלים הביטחוניים)", "הרשויות המקומיות (מרכז השלטון המקומי)", "שלוש הערים הגדולות",
         "המועצות האזוריות (מרכז המועצות האזוריות)", "המועצות הדתיות", "המוסד לביטוח לאומי", "שירות התעסוקה",
         "האוניברסיטה העברית בירושלים", "אוניברסיטת בר-אילן", "אוניברסיטת בן גוריון בנגב", "אוניברסיטת חיפה",
         "אוניברסיטת תל-אביב", "הטכניון", "מכון ויצמן למדע"

`why the State Service (Appointments) Law is not in the agreement of 18.3.2020` MEANS
    `outside the corpus` "חוק שירות המדינה (מינויים), התשי\"ט-1959, סעיף 2(6)"

§§ `1 מבוא`

@ref akn:art_1/p1
`the 2020 furlough agreement's preamble is part of it` MEANS TRUE

§§ `2 תחולת ההסכם`

-- (א): it applies to every employee of the employers that signed it who is
-- represented by the Histadrut. (ב): and to an employee of another public
-- employer (§4) that signs the accession letter of annex א'. (ג): in the
-- local authorities it does not apply to hourly employees; to project
-- employees with less than three years in that authority whose project is
-- funded 50% or more from outside; to hourly instructors; or to hourly
-- escorts on transport.
@desc An employee, as far as the agreement of 18.3.2020 asks.
DECLARE `2020 furlough employee` HAS
    `employed by an employer that signed the agreement of 18.3.2020` IS A BOOLEAN
    `employed by a public employer that signed the accession letter of 18.3.2020` IS A BOOLEAN
    `represented by the Histadrut, for 18.3.2020` IS A BOOLEAN
    `in a local authority, for 18.3.2020` IS A BOOLEAN
    `an hourly employee, instructor or escort, for 18.3.2020` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a project employee under three years, funded half or more from outside, for 18.3.2020` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref akn:art_2__para_a akn:art_2__para_b akn:art_2__para_c
GIVEN e IS A `2020 furlough employee`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the agreement of 18.3.2020 covers` e IF
        (   (    e's `employed by an employer that signed the agreement of 18.3.2020`
             AND e's `represented by the Histadrut, for 18.3.2020`)
         OR e's `employed by a public employer that signed the accession letter of 18.3.2020`)
    AND NOT (    e's `in a local authority, for 18.3.2020`
             AND (   e's `an hourly employee, instructor or escort, for 18.3.2020`
                  OR e's `a project employee under three years, funded half or more from outside, for 18.3.2020`))

`signing the accession letter of 18.3.2020` MEANS
    PARTY `the employer`
    MAY   `sign the accession letter to the agreement of 18.3.2020`

-- The same, as the Collective Agreements Law asks it (§§15–16): the kind
-- of employee it includes is the one the Histadrut represents. It does not
-- reach a teaching employee, whom הסתדרות המורים or ארגון המורים
-- represents, whoever employs him; and §23 never weighs it against a
-- teachers' agreement.
GIVEN e IS A `2020 furlough employee`
GIVETH AN `employee a collective agreement may reach`
DECIDE `the 2020 furlough employee, as the law asks` e IS
    `employee a collective agreement may reach` WITH
        `his employer is a party to the agreement`  IS e's `employed by an employer that signed the agreement of 18.3.2020`
        `his employer is represented for it by an employers' organisation that is a party` IS e's `employed by an employer that signed the agreement of 18.3.2020`
        `his employer was or became a member of an employers' organisation that is a party` IS e's `employed by an employer that signed the agreement of 18.3.2020`
        `his employer was expressly left out of the agreement` IS FALSE
        `he is of a kind of employee the agreement includes` IS e's `represented by the Histadrut, for 18.3.2020`
        `he is in an occupation or post the agreement includes` IS TRUE

§§ `3 תקופת ההסכם`

-- From 19 March 2020 to 16 April 2020, the days in (convention
-- dates.end), subject to the legislation of §8 ("תקופת ההסכם").
@ref akn:art_3/p1
`the 2020 furlough period begins` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 19 3 2020
`the 2020 furlough period ends` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 16 4 2020

GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `in the 2020 furlough period` d IF
        d `is on or after` `the 2020 furlough period begins`
    AND d `is on or before` `the 2020 furlough period ends`

`the days of the 2020 furlough period` MEANS
    DATE_SERIAL `the 2020 furlough period ends` MINUS DATE_SERIAL `the 2020 furlough period begins` PLUS 1

§§ `4 הגדרות`

-- akn:art_4/p1 "In this agreement": introduces the definitions; no rule.

-- "עובד חיוני": (1) one the manager decided, at his discretion and subject
-- to the law, is needed for work; (2) one the law obliges to work.
-- "עובד רגיל": an employee who is not an essential one.
@ref akn:art_4__hc_1 akn:art_4__hc_1__para_1 akn:art_4__hc_1__para_2 akn:art_4__hc_4
GIVEN `the manager decided he is needed` IS A BOOLEAN, `the law obliges him to work` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an essential worker in 2020` `the manager decided he is needed` `the law obliges him to work` IF
    `the manager decided he is needed` OR `the law obliges him to work`

GIVEN `the manager decided he is needed` IS A BOOLEAN, `the law obliges him to work` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a regular employee in 2020` `the manager decided he is needed` `the law obliges him to work` IF
    NOT `an essential worker in 2020` `the manager decided he is needed` `the law obliges him to work`

-- "מנהל": (1) in the civil service, the director-general of the ministry or
-- auxiliary unit, with the Civil Service Commissioner's approval; (2) in a
-- local authority, its head, director-general or secretary as the head
-- empowers, with the Ministry of the Interior's approval; (3) in an
-- institution of higher education, its director-general with the Planning
-- and Budgeting Committee chair's approval; (4) in a religious council, its
-- chair with the Ministry of Religious Services' approval; (5) at the
-- National Insurance Institute, and (6) at the Employment Service, the
-- director-general with the Minister of Labour and Welfare's approval;
-- (7) at another public employer, its director-general or the like, or the
-- most senior office-holder, with the approval of its regulator or the
-- minister responsible.
@ref akn:art_4__hc_2 akn:art_4__hc_2__para_1 akn:art_4__hc_2__para_2 akn:art_4__hc_2__para_3 akn:art_4__hc_2__para_4 akn:art_4__hc_2__para_5 akn:art_4__hc_2__para_6 akn:art_4__hc_2__para_7
DECLARE `employer of 18.3.2020` IS ONE OF
    `the civil service, of 18.3.2020`
    `a local authority, of 18.3.2020`
    `an institution of higher education, of 18.3.2020`
    `a religious council, of 18.3.2020`
    `the National Insurance Institute, of 18.3.2020`
    `the Employment Service, of 18.3.2020`
    `another public employer, of 18.3.2020`

GIVEN e IS AN `employer of 18.3.2020`
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
DECIDE `the manager of 18.3.2020 and who approves him` e IS
    CONSIDER e
    WHEN `the civil service, of 18.3.2020` THEN LIST "מנכ\"ל המשרד הממשלתי או יחידת הסמך", "נציב שירות המדינה"
    WHEN `a local authority, of 18.3.2020` THEN LIST "ראש הרשות המקומית, מנכ\"ל הרשות או מזכירה, לפי הסמכת ראש הרשות", "משרד הפנים"
    WHEN `an institution of higher education, of 18.3.2020` THEN LIST "מנכ\"ל המוסד להשכלה גבוהה", "יו\"ר ות\"ת"
    WHEN `a religious council, of 18.3.2020` THEN LIST "יו\"ר המועצה הדתית", "המשרד לשירותי דת"
    WHEN `the National Insurance Institute, of 18.3.2020` THEN LIST "מנכ\"ל המוסד לביטוח לאומי", "שר העבודה והרווחה"
    WHEN `the Employment Service, of 18.3.2020` THEN LIST "מנכ\"ל שירות התעסוקה", "שר העבודה והרווחה"
    WHEN `another public employer, of 18.3.2020` THEN LIST "המנכ\"ל, בעל תפקיד מקביל, או בעל התפקיד הבכיר ביותר בהנהלה", "הגורם המאסדר או השר האחראי"

-- "מעסיק ציבורי": (1) a budgeted body as §21 of the Budget Foundations Law
-- defines it, and (2) a health corporation as §21 defines it; (3) a
-- supported body as §32 defines it (both imported); (4) an educational
-- institution whose budget the government takes part in, directly or not;
-- (5) a recognised institution of higher education under §9 of the Council
-- for Higher Education Law, or one with a permit under §21א, whose budget
-- the government took part in, directly or not, at 25% or more in 2019.
-- Which a body is, beside §§21 and 32, is an input.
@ref akn:art_4__hc_3 akn:art_4__hc_3__para_1 akn:art_4__hc_3__para_2 akn:art_4__hc_3__para_3 akn:art_4__hc_3__para_4 akn:art_4__hc_3__para_5
@desc A body, as far as the definition of a public employer of 18.3.2020 asks.
DECLARE `body of 18.3.2020` HAS
    `as the Budget Foundations Law tells bodies apart, of 18.3.2020` IS AN `employing body`
    `a health corporation, of 18.3.2020` IS A BOOLEAN
    `an educational institution the government funds, of 18.3.2020` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a recognised or permitted institution of higher education, of 18.3.2020` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the government's share of its 2019 budget, of 18.3.2020` IS A NUMBER

GIVEN b IS A `body of 18.3.2020`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a public employer of 18.3.2020` b IF
       `is a budgeted body` (b's `as the Budget Foundations Law tells bodies apart, of 18.3.2020`)
    OR b's `a health corporation, of 18.3.2020`
    OR `is a supported body` (b's `as the Budget Foundations Law tells bodies apart, of 18.3.2020`)
    OR b's `an educational institution the government funds, of 18.3.2020`
    OR (    b's `a recognised or permitted institution of higher education, of 18.3.2020`
        AND b's `the government's share of its 2019 budget, of 18.3.2020` AT LEAST 25%)

`why the Council for Higher Education Law is not in the agreement of 18.3.2020` MEANS
    `outside the corpus` "חוק המועצה להשכלה גבוהה, התשי\"ח-1958, סעיפים 9 ו־21א"

§§ `5 יציאה לחופשה`

-- ¶1: in the period, 19.3.2020–16.4.2020, every regular employee is on
-- leave as follows. (א): while he has a positive balance of rest-leave days
-- — every kind of yearly leave, whatever its name (special, temporary), but
-- not days of choice or internal leave — the leave is out of that balance.
-- (ב): one without a positive balance is on leave too, as an advance on the
-- rest-leave days (that only accumulate) he will be owed after the period.
-- (ד): this changes no existing rule on charging the leave balance. A day
-- of the period is charged as a day of leave by those rules; how many are
-- charged is an input.
@ref akn:art_5/p1 akn:art_5__para_a akn:art_5__para_b akn:art_5__para_d
DECLARE `kind of leave of 18.3.2020` IS ONE OF
    `yearly rest leave, of 18.3.2020`
    `special or temporary leave, of 18.3.2020`
    `days of choice, of 18.3.2020`
    `internal leave, of 18.3.2020`

GIVEN k IS A `kind of leave of 18.3.2020`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the furlough of 18.3.2020 is charged to` k IF
    NOT (k EQUALS `days of choice, of 18.3.2020` OR k EQUALS `internal leave, of 18.3.2020`)

GIVEN `his balance of rest-leave days` IS A NUMBER, `days of the period charged as leave` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `furlough days out of his balance, of 18.3.2020` `his balance of rest-leave days` `days of the period charged as leave` IS
    min (`not below zero` `his balance of rest-leave days`) `days of the period charged as leave`

GIVEN `his balance of rest-leave days` IS A NUMBER, `days of the period charged as leave` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `furlough days as an advance, of 18.3.2020` `his balance of rest-leave days` `days of the period charged as leave` IS
    `days of the period charged as leave` MINUS `furlough days out of his balance, of 18.3.2020` `his balance of rest-leave days` `days of the period charged as leave`

-- (ג): for the students' scale, using the leave days is subject to §6.2 of
-- the students' agreement of 18.4.2016 (outside the corpus).
@ref akn:art_5__para_c
`why the students' agreement is not in the agreement of 18.3.2020` MEANS
    `outside the corpus` "ההסכם הקיבוצי בעניין הסטודנטים מיום 18.4.2016, סעיף 6.2"

-- (ה): the accounting for leave taken under (ב) may be made through the
-- vacation fund of §6, by rules still to be set.
@ref akn:art_5__para_e
`the advance of 18.3.2020 may be settled through the vacation fund` MEANS TRUE

-- (ו): where a concentrated leave starting on the eve of Passover 5780 is
-- the custom ("החופשה המרוכזת"), nothing changes in it, including the
-- charging of the balance under it.
@ref akn:art_5__para_f
`the agreement of 18.3.2020 changes the concentrated Passover leave` MEANS FALSE

-- (ז): an employee under an arrangement that he is absent with pay in July–
-- August 2020 may be called by the employer to work then — or, if his
-- workplace is closed then for these reasons, at another time agreed — in
-- all or part of that absence, the school year 5780's extension included,
-- for no more days than he was on leave in the period. ¶2: those days come
-- in place of charging as many leave days under §5, provided no pay is
-- doubled.
@ref akn:art_5__para_g
`calling the employee back in July–August 2020` MEANS
    PARTY `the employer`
    MAY   `call the employee to work in July–August 2020 in place of the furlough days`

GIVEN `days called to work` IS A NUMBER, `days on leave in the period` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `days he may be called back for, of 18.3.2020` `days called to work` `days on leave in the period` IS
    min `days called to work` `days on leave in the period`

@ref akn:art_5__para_g/p2
GIVEN `days charged as leave` IS A NUMBER, `days called to work` IS A NUMBER, `days on leave in the period` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `days left charged after the call-back, of 18.3.2020` `days charged as leave` `days called to work` `days on leave in the period` IS
    `not below zero` (`days charged as leave` MINUS `days he may be called back for, of 18.3.2020` `days called to work` `days on leave in the period`)

-- (ח): none of this applies to a regular employee for a time he is on
-- unpaid leave that began before the period, on reserve duty, or in a
-- period of birth and parenthood under the Women's Work Law (whether he
-- is in it is a fact of the case). ¶2: the Histadrut may ask the employers
-- to apply it to all or some of the employees sent on unpaid leave in the
-- week before it began.
@ref akn:art_5__para_h
GIVEN `on unpaid leave begun before the period` IS A BOOLEAN, `on reserve duty` IS A BOOLEAN, `in birth and parenthood` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `§5 of 18.3.2020 applies to him for the time` `on unpaid leave begun before the period` `on reserve duty` `in birth and parenthood` IF
    NOT (`on unpaid leave begun before the period` OR `on reserve duty` OR `in birth and parenthood`)

-- The Women's Work Law (imported): (ח) leaves the birth and parenthood
-- period out of the furlough, so no day of it is charged to the leave
-- balance or advanced on it: the period stays the law's, in which the
-- employee is not at work (§8), and it takes from the balance, a right
-- that grows with seniority, nothing (§6(ט)). The floor is met.
`(ח) leaves the birth and parenthood period to the Women's Work Law` MEANS
        NOT `§5 of 18.3.2020 applies to him for the time` FALSE FALSE TRUE
    AND NOT `the employer may have the employee work in the birth and parenthood period`
    AND `the birth and parenthood period harms no right that turns on seniority`
#ASSERT `(ח) leaves the birth and parenthood period to the Women's Work Law`

@ref akn:art_5__para_h/p2
`asking to bring in those sent on unpaid leave` MEANS
    PARTY `the New General Histadrut`
    MAY   `ask that the agreement of 18.3.2020 apply to employees sent on unpaid leave the week before`

-- (ט): in view of the exceptional circumstances a regular employee has no
-- sick pay for the period; but a sick note issued before 15.3.2020 (not
-- included) for days in the period gives sick pay. The rest of the clause
-- is illegible in the corpus ("[לא קריא]") save that sick notes of
-- hospitalisation or a serious illness are discussed in the follow-up
-- committee of §7.
@ref akn:art_5__para_i
GIVEN `a sick note for the day issued on` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `sick pay for a day of the period, of 18.3.2020` `a sick note for the day issued on` IF
    CONSIDER `a sick note for the day issued on`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST i THEN DATE_SERIAL i LESS THAN DATE_SERIAL (DATE_FROM_DMY 15 3 2020)

`what §5(ט) of 18.3.2020 says of the notes issued before 15.3.2020` MEANS
    `the text is missing` "סעיף 5(ט) להסכם 18.3.2020: המילים שאחרי \"כמזכות בדמי מחלה, והן\" ועד \"אשפוז\", כפי שהקורפוס מסמן [לא קריא]"

-- The Sick Pay Law (imported), §1: an employee whose payment for a period
-- of illness a collective agreement regulates — this one, for the period —
-- is not "an employee" for the law, so §§2 to 6 do not reach him, and §12(ב)
-- keeps what the agreements give. No sick pay for days already his
-- vacation is (ט)'s own arrangement, and the law sets no floor under it;
-- §4א, which does reach him, limits a dismissal, of which (ט) says nothing.
`the furlough's sick-pay rule is under no floor of the Sick Pay Law` MEANS
        NOT `an employee as section 1 of the Sick Pay Law means` TRUE
    AND NOT `sick pay for a day of the period, of 18.3.2020` NOTHING
    AND `section 4א reaches an employee whose sick pay a collective agreement regulates`
#ASSERT `the furlough's sick-pay rule is under no floor of the Sick Pay Law`

-- The Annual Leave Law (imported), §5(א)(4) and (ב): a day the employee
-- cannot work for illness is not counted among the days of leave; where
-- it falls in the leave, the leave stops for it and is made up. §33 makes
-- a State employee like any other. The agreement sends every regular
-- employee on leave for the period, charged to his balance (¶1, (א)–(ב));
-- (ח) takes out reserve duty and birth and parenthood, two of §5(א)'s
-- days, but not illness; and (ט) gives no sick pay for a sick note issued
-- from 15.3.2020 on, so the days of an illness begun in the period stay
-- days of leave charged to the balance. F-framework-2020-03-a: below the
-- floor. The law governs (`what stands under section 38 of the Annual
-- Leave Law`; convention instruments.statute-floor), and the balance is
-- not charged for the days of illness.
`the furlough charges as leave a day of illness section 5 of the Annual Leave Law does not count` MEANS
        `the furlough of 18.3.2020 is charged to` `yearly rest leave, of 18.3.2020`
    AND `§5 of 18.3.2020 applies to him for the time` FALSE FALSE FALSE
    AND NOT `sick pay for a day of the period, of 18.3.2020` (JUST (DATE_FROM_DMY 25 3 2020))
    AND `furlough days out of his balance, of 18.3.2020` 20 10 EQUALS 10
    AND `days of leave the period gives under section 5` 10 10 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the furlough charges as leave a day of illness section 5 of the Annual Leave Law does not count`

-- (א) leaves the days of choice out of what the period is charged to, so
-- the day §6(ב) lets the employee choose is still his to take.
#ASSERT NOT `the furlough of 18.3.2020 is charged to` `days of choice, of 18.3.2020`

`discussing the hospitalisation notes` MEANS
    PARTY `the follow-up committee`
    MUST  `discuss a sick note of hospitalisation or serious illness in the furlough period`

§§ `6–8 קרן ימי חופשה, ועדת מעקב ויישום`

-- §6: out of mutual guarantee, and by understandings with each employer, a
-- vacation-days fund is set up at each, to help employees without enough
-- leave days to use them in the period, by rules to be set in a collective
-- agreement (not in the corpus).
@ref akn:art_6/p1
`setting up the vacation-days fund` MEANS
    PARTY `the employer`
    MUST  `set up a vacation-days fund under the agreement of 18.3.2020`

`the rules of the vacation-days fund of 18.3.2020` MEANS
    `set elsewhere` "הסכם קיבוצי שיעגן את כללי קרן ימי החופשה (סעיף 6 להסכם 18.3.2020)"

-- §7: a follow-up committee of the wages commissioner and the chair of the
-- trade-union department follows and helps carry it out and decides
-- disputes over it; its decisions are final and bind the parties.
@ref akn:art_7/p1
`the 2020 furlough follow-up committee` MEANS
    PARTY `the follow-up committee`
    MAY   `decide disputes over the agreement of 18.3.2020`

-- §8: the government announces its intention to act to legislate, by
-- primary or secondary legislation, to carry the agreement out and anchor
-- it and avoid a clash with the law, as far as it can: an intention, not a
-- duty.
@ref akn:art_8/p1
`legislating the agreement of 18.3.2020` MEANS
    PARTY `the State`
    MAY   `act to legislate the agreement of 18.3.2020`

