-- akn:att_1__hc_1/t1 The date and the signature for the employer, left blank; no rule.

-- ¶6: the employer gives notice of its wish to join the agreement: the
-- form §2(ב) names.
@ref akn:att_1__hc_1/p6
`the accession letter of 18.3.2020 is the form of §2(ב)` MEANS TRUE

§§ `דוגמאות`

`a clerk of the State in March 2020` MEANS `2020 furlough employee` WITH
    `employed by an employer that signed the agreement of 18.3.2020` IS TRUE
    `employed by a public employer that signed the accession letter of 18.3.2020` IS FALSE
    `represented by the Histadrut, for 18.3.2020` IS TRUE
    `in a local authority, for 18.3.2020` IS FALSE
    `an hourly employee, instructor or escort, for 18.3.2020` IS FALSE
    `a project employee under three years, funded half or more from outside, for 18.3.2020` IS FALSE
`a teacher of the State in March 2020` MEANS `2020 furlough employee` WITH
    `employed by an employer that signed the agreement of 18.3.2020` IS TRUE
    `employed by a public employer that signed the accession letter of 18.3.2020` IS FALSE
    `represented by the Histadrut, for 18.3.2020` IS FALSE
    `in a local authority, for 18.3.2020` IS FALSE
    `an hourly employee, instructor or escort, for 18.3.2020` IS FALSE
    `a project employee under three years, funded half or more from outside, for 18.3.2020` IS FALSE
`an hourly escort of a local authority in March 2020` MEANS `2020 furlough employee` WITH
    `employed by an employer that signed the agreement of 18.3.2020` IS TRUE
    `employed by a public employer that signed the accession letter of 18.3.2020` IS FALSE
    `represented by the Histadrut, for 18.3.2020` IS TRUE
    `in a local authority, for 18.3.2020` IS TRUE
    `an hourly employee, instructor or escort, for 18.3.2020` IS TRUE
    `a project employee under three years, funded half or more from outside, for 18.3.2020` IS FALSE

-- §2: the clerk is in it; a State teacher, whom the Histadrut does not
-- represent, is not — by the agreement and by the law; nor an hourly
-- escort of a local authority.
#ASSERT `the agreement of 18.3.2020 covers` `a clerk of the State in March 2020`
#ASSERT NOT `the agreement of 18.3.2020 covers` `a teacher of the State in March 2020`
#ASSERT NOT `the agreement of 18.3.2020 covers` `an hourly escort of a local authority in March 2020`
#ASSERT NOT `the collective agreement applies to the employee` `a general collective agreement` (`the 2020 furlough employee, as the law asks` `a teacher of the State in March 2020`)
#ASSERT NOT `the collective agreement applies to the employee` `a special collective agreement` (`the 2020 furlough employee, as the law asks` `a teacher of the State in March 2020`)
#ASSERT `the collective agreement applies to the employee` `a special collective agreement` (`the 2020 furlough employee, as the law asks` `a clerk of the State in March 2020`)

-- §3: 29 days, 19.3.2020–16.4.2020.
#ASSERT `the days of the 2020 furlough period` EQUALS 29
#ASSERT `in the 2020 furlough period` (DATE_FROM_DMY 16 4 2020)
#ASSERT NOT `in the 2020 furlough period` (DATE_FROM_DMY 18 3 2020)

-- §4: a regular employee is one neither the manager nor the law calls to
-- work. A local authority is a public employer by §21; a university with
-- 30% of its 2019 budget from the government is, one with 20% is not.
#ASSERT `a regular employee in 2020` FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `a regular employee in 2020` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `a regular employee in 2020` FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT `a public employer of 18.3.2020` (`body of 18.3.2020` `a local authority` FALSE FALSE FALSE 0)
#ASSERT `a public employer of 18.3.2020` (`body of 18.3.2020` `another employer` FALSE FALSE TRUE (30%))
#ASSERT NOT `a public employer of 18.3.2020` (`body of 18.3.2020` `another employer` FALSE FALSE TRUE (20%))
#ASSERT count (`the manager of 18.3.2020 and who approves him` `the civil service, of 18.3.2020`) EQUALS 2

-- §5: 20 days of the period charged as leave, against a balance of 12 —
-- 12 out of it and 8 as an advance; with 30 days' balance, all 20 out of
-- it. Called back for 25 days in July, only 20 replace the charge, and
-- nothing is left charged; called back for 5, 15 are. Days of choice are
-- not charged. A sick note of 10.3.2020 gives sick pay; one of 16.3.2020,
-- or none, does not.
#ASSERT `furlough days out of his balance, of 18.3.2020` 12 20 EQUALS 12
#ASSERT `furlough days as an advance, of 18.3.2020` 12 20 EQUALS 8
#ASSERT `furlough days as an advance, of 18.3.2020` 30 20 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `days left charged after the call-back, of 18.3.2020` 20 25 20 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `days left charged after the call-back, of 18.3.2020` 20 5 20 EQUALS 15
#ASSERT NOT `the furlough of 18.3.2020 is charged to` `days of choice, of 18.3.2020`
#ASSERT `the furlough of 18.3.2020 is charged to` `special or temporary leave, of 18.3.2020`
#ASSERT `sick pay for a day of the period, of 18.3.2020` (JUST (DATE_FROM_DMY 10 3 2020))
#ASSERT NOT `sick pay for a day of the period, of 18.3.2020` (JUST (DATE_FROM_DMY 16 3 2020))
#ASSERT NOT `sick pay for a day of the period, of 18.3.2020` NOTHING
#ASSERT NOT `§5 of 18.3.2020 applies to him for the time` FALSE TRUE FALSE
